<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 19 February, from 197 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/septimius-severus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">197 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,829 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Septimius Severus defeats Clodius Albinus at Lugdunum</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lyon">Lyon</a>, Severus won a hard-fought battle against his rival for the throne, said to have involved some 300,000 men. Albinus died, leaving Severus sole emperor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1473">1473 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">553 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nicolaus Copernicus is born in Toruń</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Copernicus's '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/de-revolutionibus-orbium-coelestium">On the Revolutions of the Heavenly Spheres</a>', published as he died in 1543, placed the Sun rather than the Earth at the centre. It became a starting point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scientific-revolution">Scientific Revolution</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scientific-revolution">Scientific Revolution</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1714">1714 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">312 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Swedish and Russian armies fight the Battle of Napue</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Swedish and Russian armies fought at the villages of Napue and Laurola in Isokyrö parish, Ostrobothnia. It was the final land battle of the Finnish campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1807">1807 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Aaron Burr arrested for treason in Alabama</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former Vice-President was seized near Wakefield, accused of plotting to found an independent nation in the West. He was acquitted that September, but his political career was over.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1878">1878 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">148 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edison receives a patent for the phonograph</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edison's tinfoil phonograph was the first machine able to record sound and play it back. Its first words were 'Mary had a little lamb'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1915">1915 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied fleet begins bombarding the Dardanelles forts</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French warships opened fire on Ottoman forts guarding the straits, hoping to force a way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. The naval effort failed in March, leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli">Gallipoli</a> landings.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt signs Executive Order 9066</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The order allowed the military to exclude people from designated areas, leading to the internment of about 120,000 Japanese Americans. Congress apologised and paid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-reparations">reparations</a> in 1988.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US Marines land on Iwo Jima</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The 36-day battle killed nearly 7,000 Americans and almost all of the 21,000 Japanese defenders. Joe Rosenthal's photograph of the flag raising on Mount Suribachi became an icon.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 19 February <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nicolaus-copernicus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nicolaus-copernicus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nicolaus Copernicus</span><span class="tp">1473–1543</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sven-hedin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sven-hedin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sven Hedin</span><span class="tp">1865–1952</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/alvaro-obregon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/alvaro-obregon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Álvaro Obregón</span><span class="tp">1880–1928</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pim-fortuyn"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pim-fortuyn.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pim Fortuyn</span><span class="tp">1948–2002</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cristina-fernandez-de-kirchner"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cristina-fernandez-de-kirchner.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cristina Fernández de Kirchner</span><span class="tp">b. 1953</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
